corr('P000917','Carry-out: stratification subscripts',r'\(X_{2n}\supset X_{2n-2}\supset X_{n-3}\supset X_{n-4}\).',r'Keep consistent real-dimensional subscripts, such as \(X_{2n-i}\); for a complex stratification odd levels may repeat.','Both transcriptions and original scan reproduce the abrupt 2n to n change. This belongs to Fuchs on22September1980, separately inventoried, not to Zakharov record488.')
corr('P000917','Carry-out: allowable-chain equation',r'\(\dim(\sigma_j\cap X_{2n-i})=j-2i\).',r'\(\dim(|c|\cap X_{2n-i})\le j-i+\bar p(i)\), with the separate boundary condition \(\dim(|\partial c|\cap X_{2n-i})\le j-1-i+\bar p(i)\).','The original scan clearly has equality and j-2i. Goresky--MacPherson1977/1980 definitions give the corrected perversity bounds. This is a faithful mathematical error in next-year spillover.')
corr('P000917','Carry-out: unspecified L2 comparison',r'Intersection homology coincides with \(L_2\)-cohomology.',r'Specify the metric, regular locus, coefficients and differential domain; the arithmetic Zucker theorem is one precise partial match, not a metric-free universal statement.','The scan gives none of those choices. Looijenga1988,p3 supplies the arithmetic metric/local-system hypotheses. Boundary inventory B05 preserves the unresolved identification.',typ='ambiguity')
